#+TITLE: Captain's Bridge — org-llm vital signs
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: captains-bridge
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:captain:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# The admin-pulse dashboard owned by =@picard=. Six charts, one per
# vital sign, single-column layout. Every metric expression here is
# verbatim from =org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml= so the dashboard and
# the =@analyst=-style agents agree on numbers byte-for-byte.

* Agent fan-out heatmap
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Distinct downstream agents that each =agent_from= has talked to —
the proxy-vs-manager dominance lens. A fat row on =@proxy= means the
manager is not earning its keep; a fat row on =@picard= means
delegation is healthy.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name agent_fan_out_heatmap :metric agent_fan_out :group_by [agent_from, agent_to]
SELECT agent_from, agent_to, COUNT(DISTINCT agent_to) AS agent_fan_out
FROM crew_log
GROUP BY agent_from, agent_to
#+END_SRC

* Model cost & latency
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Mean wall-clock duration of LLM calls bucketed by =call_kind= ×
=model=. The 87× chat/embed gap should jump out instantly; new
spikes flag slow models or context-bloat regressions.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name model_cost_latency :metric llm_avg_ms :group_by [call_kind, model]
SELECT call_kind, model, AVG(duration_ms) AS llm_avg_ms
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY call_kind, model
#+END_SRC

* Error rate by model
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Fraction of LLM calls whose outcome wasn't =ok=, per model. Catches
silent breakage like the phi3.5 50/50 failure pattern from the
2026-05-06 tier-1 probe.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name error_rate_by_model :metric llm_error_rate :group_by [model]
SELECT model, AVG(CASE WHEN outcome != 'ok' THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS llm_error_rate
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY model
#+END_SRC

* Captain's-log heatmap
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

When activity happens, by category. Rows = =hist_kind= (capture,
chat, agent, …), columns = day. Sparse rows or sudden bands flag
either a quiet day or a runaway agent loop.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name captains_log_heatmap :metric hist_events :group_by [hist_kind, hist_day]
SELECT kind AS hist_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(*) AS hist_events
FROM history
GROUP BY kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Memory-pressure timeline
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Fraction of sensor readings at =watch=, =alert=, or =critical=, per
status × day. The system-health pulse — when this trends up the
captain should drill into =@geordi='s console for root cause.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name memory_pressure_timeline :metric probe_alert_rate :group_by [probe_status, sensor_day]
SELECT status AS probe_status, date(ts, 'unixepoch') AS sensor_day, AVG(CASE WHEN status IN ('watch','alert','critical') THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS probe_alert_rate
FROM sensor_log
GROUP BY status, date(ts, 'unixepoch')
#+END_SRC

* History kind drift
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Distinct =hist_kind= values per day — the new-event-kind detector.
A bump means a new subsystem started writing to history (worth
naming); a drop means something stopped (worth investigating).

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name history_kind_drift :metric hist_kind_count :group_by [hist_day]
SELECT substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(DISTINCT kind) AS hist_kind_count
FROM history
GROUP BY substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

# Run:
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/org-llm-captains-bridge.org.example \
#       --emit-only /tmp/captains-bridge.zip
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/org-llm-captains-bridge.org.example \
#       --post http://localhost:8088
